In determining which law or which contract is to be observed, where two laws or two contracts accidentally interfere; Grotius says, that the latter, is to be observed in preference to the former. But then he proposes this as a rule, which is only to be applied, when all others fail, or when all other circumstances are equal; so that the point could not be settled without the help of this rule. The other rules, which he lays down for this purpose, are these, which follow.
